// cdgmm This function performs the matrix-matrix multiplication C={A×diag(X)if mode == CUBLAS_SIDE_RIGHTdiag(X)×Aif mode == [SideLeft] where A and C are matrices stored in column-major format with dimensions m×n .
//
// X is a vector of size n if mode == [SideRight] and of size m if mode == [SideLeft]. X is gathered from one-dimensional array x with stride incx. The absolute value of incx is the stride and the sign of incx is direction of the stride. If incx is positive, then we forward x from the first element. Otherwise, we backward x from the last element. The formula of X is Xj={x [j×incx]if incx≥0x[(χ−1)×|incx|−j×|incx|]if incx<0 where χ=m if mode == [SideLeft] and χ=n if mode == [SideRight]. Example 1: if the user wants to perform diag(diag(B))×A , then incx=ldb+1 where ldb is leading dimension of matrix B, either row-major or column-major. Example 2: if the user wants to perform α×A , then there are two choices, either cublasgeam() with *beta == 0 and transa == [OpN] or cublasdgmm() with incx == 0 and x [0] == alpha. The operation is out-of-place. The in-place only works if lda == ldc. The possible error values returned by this function and their meanings are listed below.
//
//   - handle: Handle to the cuBLAS library context
//   - mode: Left multiply if mode == [SideLeft] or right multiply if mode == [SideRight]
//   - m: Number of rows of matrix A and C
//   - n: Number of columns of matrix A and C
//   - A: < type > array of dimensions lda x n with lda >= max(1, m)
//   - lda: Leading dimension of two-dimensional array used to store the matrix A
//   - x: One-dimensional < type > array of size abs(incx) x m if mode == [SideLeft] and abs(incx) x n if mode == [SideRight]
//   - incx: Stride of one-dimensional array x
//   - C: < type > array of dimensions ldc x n with ldc >= max(1, m)
//   - ldc: Leading dimension of a two-dimensional array used to store the matrix C
//
// Returns:
//   - StatusExecutionFailed: The function failed to launch on the GPU
//   - StatusInvalidValue: - If m < 0 or n < 0, or - if mode is not one of [SideLeft] and [SideRight], or - if lda < max(1, m), or - if ldc < max(1, m)
//   - StatusNotInitialized: The library was not initialized
//   - StatusSuccess: The operation completed successfully
//
// Wraps cublasCdgmm.
func cdgmm(handle Handle, mode SideMode, m int32, n int32, A *Complex64, lda int32, x *Complex64, incx int32, C *Complex64, ldc int32) error {
	if err := checkLibSym("cublasCdgmm"); err != nil {
		return err
	}
	return toError(fncdgmm(handle, mode, m, n, A, lda, x, incx, C, ldc))
}

