// Create This function initializes the cuBLAS library and creates a handle to an opaque structure holding the cuBLAS library context.
//
// The cuBLAS library context is tied to the current CUDA device. To use the library on multiple devices, one cuBLAS handle needs to be created for each device. See also cuBLAS Context. For a given device, multiple cuBLAS handles with different configurations can be created. For multi-threaded applications that use the same device from different threads, the recommended programming model is to create one cuBLAS handle per thread and use that cuBLAS handle for the entire life of the thread. Because [Create] allocates some internal resources and the release of those resources by calling [Handle.Destroy] will implicitly call cudaDeviceSynchronize(), it is recommended to minimize the number of times these functions are called.
//
// Wraps cublasCreate_v2.
func Create() (Handle, error) {
	if err := checkLibSym("cublasCreate_v2"); err != nil {
		var zero Handle
		return zero, err
	}
	var out Handle
	if err := toError(fnCreate(&out)); err != nil {
		var zero Handle
		return zero, err
	}
	return out, nil
}

// crot This function applies Givens rotation matrix (i.e., rotation in the x,y plane counter-clockwise by angle defined by cos(alpha)=c, sin(alpha)=s): G=(cs−sc) to vectors x and y.
