//
//   - handle: Handle to the cuBLAS library context
//   - trans: Operation op( Ai) that is non- or (conj.) transpose
//   - m: Number of rows of matrix Ai
//   - n: Number of columns of matrix Ai
//   - alpha: < type > scalar used for multiplication
//   - Aarray: Array of pointers to < type > array, with each array of dim. lda x n with lda >= max(1, m).All pointers must meet certain alignment criteria. Please see below for details
//   - lda: Leading dimension of two-dimensional array used to store each matrix Ai
//   - xarray: Array of pointers to < type > array, with each dimension n if trans == [OpN] and m otherwise.All pointers must meet certain alignment criteria. Please see below for details
//   - incx: Stride of each one-dimensional array xi
//   - beta: < type > scalar used for multiplication. If beta == 0, y does not have to be a valid input
//   - yarray: Array of pointers to < type > array. It has dimensions m if trans == [OpN] and n otherwise. Vectors yi should not overlap; otherwise, undefined behavior is expected.All pointers must meet certain alignment criteria. Please see below for details
//   - incy: Stride of each one-dimensional array yi
//   - batchCount: Number of pointers contained in Aarray, xarray and yarray
//
// Returns:
//   - StatusExecutionFailed: The function failed to launch on the GPU
//   - StatusInvalidValue: m < 0, n < 0, or batchCount < 0
