// dotEx These functions support the 64-bit Integer Interface.
//
// These functions are an API generalization of the routines cublasdot() and cublasdotc() where input data, output data and compute type can be specified independently. Note: cublasdotc() is dot product conjugated, cublasdotu() is dot product unconjugated. This function computes the dot product of vectors x and y. Hence, the result is ∑i=1n(xk×yj) where k=1+(i−1)∗incx and j=1+(i−1)∗incy . Notice that in the first equation the conjugate of the element of vector x should be used if the function name ends in character ‘c’ and that the last two equations reflect 1-based indexing used for compatibility with Fortran. The datatypes combinations currently supported for [Handle.DotEx] and [Handle.DotcEx] are listed below: The possible error values returned by this function and their meanings are listed in the following table: For references please refer to NETLIB documentation: sdot(), ddot(), cdotu(), cdotc(), zdotu(), zdotc()
//
//   - handle: Handle to the cuBLAS library context
//   - n: Number of elements in the vectors x and y
//   - x: < type > vector with n elements
//   - xType: Enumerant specifying the datatype of vector x
//   - incx: Stride between consecutive elements of x
//   - y: < type > vector with n elements
//   - yType: Enumerant specifying the datatype of vector y
//   - incy: Stride between consecutive elements of y
//   - result: The resulting dot product, which is set to 0 if n <= 0
//   - resultType: Enumerant specifying the datatype of the result
//   - executionType: Enumerant specifying the datatype in which the computation is executed
//
// Returns:
//   - StatusAllocFailed: The reduction buffer could not be allocated.
//   - StatusExecutionFailed: The function failed to launch on the GPU.
//   - StatusInvalidValue: xType or yType or resultType or executionType is not supported.
//   - StatusNotInitialized: The library was not initialized.
//   - StatusNotSupported: The combination of the parameters xType, yType, resultType and executionType is not supported.
//   - StatusSuccess: The operation completed successfully.
//
// Wraps cublasDotEx.
func dotEx(handle Handle, n int32, x uintptr, xType DataType, incx int32, y uintptr, yType DataType, incy int32, result uintptr, resultType DataType, executionType DataType) error {
	if err := checkLibSym("cublasDotEx"); err != nil {
		return err
	}
	return toError(fndotEx(handle, n, x, xType, incx, y, yType, incy, result, resultType, executionType))
}

