// ssbmv This function performs the symmetric banded matrix-vector multiplication y=αAx+βy where A is a n×n symmetric banded matrix with k subdiagonals and superdiagonals, x and y are vectors, and α and β are scalars.
//
// If uplo == [FillModeLower] then the symmetric banded matrix A is stored column by column, with the main diagonal of the matrix stored in row 1, the first subdiagonal in row 2 (starting at first position), the second subdiagonal in row 3 (starting at first position), etc. So that in general, the element A(i,j) is stored in the memory location A(1+i-j,j) for j=1,…,n and i∈[j,min(m,j+k)] . Also, the elements in the array A that do not conceptually correspond to the elements in the banded matrix (the bottom right k×k triangle) are not referenced. If uplo == [FillModeUpper] then the symmetric banded matrix A is stored column by column, with the main diagonal of the matrix stored in row k + 1, the first superdiagonal in row k (starting at second position), the second superdiagonal in row k-1 (starting at third position), etc. So that in general, the element A(i,j) is stored in the memory location A(1+k+i-j,j) for j=1,…,n and i∈[max(1,j−k),j] . Also, the elements in the array A that do not conceptually correspond to the elements in the banded matrix (the top left k×k triangle) are not referenced. The possible error values returned by this function and their meanings are listed below. For references please refer to NETLIB documentation: ssbmv(), dsbmv()
//
//   - handle: Handle to the cuBLAS library context
//   - uplo: Indicates if matrix A lower or upper part is stored, the other symmetric part is not referenced and is inferred from the stored elements
//   - n: Number of rows and columns of matrix A
//   - k: Number of sub- and super-diagonals of matrix A
//   - alpha: < type > scalar used for multiplication
//   - A: < type > array of dimension lda x n with lda >= k + 1
//   - lda: Leading dimension of two-dimensional array used to store matrix A
//   - x: < type > vector with n elements
//   - incx: Stride between consecutive elements of x
//   - beta: < type > scalar used for multiplication. If beta == 0 then y does not have to be a valid input
//   - y: < type > vector with n elements
//   - incy: Stride between consecutive elements of y
//
// Returns:
//   - StatusExecutionFailed: The function failed to launch on the GPU
//   - StatusInvalidValue: - If n < 0 or k < 0, or - if incx == 0 or incy == 0, or - if uplo is not one of [FillModeLower] and [FillModeUpper], or - if alpha or beta are NULL, or - if lda < (1 + k)
//   - StatusNotInitialized: The library was not initialized
//   - StatusSuccess: The operation completed successfully
//
// Wraps cublasSsbmv_v2.
func ssbmv(handle Handle, uplo FillMode, n int32, k int32, alpha *float32, A *float32, lda int32, x *float32, incx int32, beta *float32, y *float32, incy int32) error {
	if err := checkLibSym("cublasSsbmv_v2"); err != nil {
		return err
	}
	return toError(fnssbmv(handle, uplo, n, k, alpha, A, lda, x, incx, beta, y, incy))
}

