// ztpmv This function performs the triangular packed matrix-vector multiplication x=op(A)x where A is a triangular matrix stored in packed format, and x is a vector.
//
// Also, for matrix A op(A)={Aif trans == CUBLAS_OP_NATif trans == CUBLAS_OP_TAHif trans == [OpC] If uplo == [FillModeLower] then the elements in the lower triangular part of the triangular matrix A are packed together column by column without gaps, so that the element A(i,j) is stored in the memory location AP [i+((2*n-j+1)*j)/2] for j=1,…,n and i≥j . Consequently, the packed format requires only n(n+1)2 elements for storage. If uplo == [FillModeUpper] then the elements in the upper triangular part of the triangular matrix A are packed together column by column without gaps, so that the element A(i,j) is stored in the memory location AP [i+(j*(j+1))/2] for A(i,j) and i≤j . Consequently, the packed format requires only n(n+1)2 elements for storage. The possible error values returned by this function and their meanings are listed below. For references please refer to NETLIB documentation: stpmv(), dtpmv(), ctpmv(), ztpmv()
//
//   - handle: Handle to the cuBLAS library context
//   - uplo: Indicates if matrix A lower or upper part is stored, the other part is not referenced and is inferred from the stored elements
//   - trans: Operation op( A) that is non- or (conj.) transpose
//   - diag: Indicates if the elements on the main diagonal of matrix A are unity and should not be accessed
//   - n: Number of rows and columns of matrix A
//   - AP: < type > array with A stored in packed format
//   - x: < type > vector with n elements
//   - incx: Stride between consecutive elements of x
//
// Returns:
//   - StatusAllocFailed: The allocation of internal scratch memory failed
//   - StatusExecutionFailed: The function failed to launch on the GPU
//   - StatusInvalidValue: - If n < 0, or - if incx == 0, or - if trans is not one of [OpN], [OpT] and [OpC], or - if uplo is not one of [FillModeLower] and [FillModeUpper], or - if diag is not one of [DiagUnit] and [DiagNonUnit]
//   - StatusNotInitialized: The library was not initialized
//   - StatusSuccess: The operation completed successfully
//
// Wraps cublasZtpmv_v2.
func ztpmv(handle Handle, uplo FillMode, trans Operation, diag DiagType, n int32, AP *Complex128, x *Complex128, incx int32) error {
	if err := checkLibSym("cublasZtpmv_v2"); err != nil {
		return err
	}
	return toError(fnztpmv(handle, uplo, trans, diag, n, AP, x, incx))
}

